<section image-layout="blank" id="0xg5rYGE5Z" vertical-align="end" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.38" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/WMImjznaq1xA7ohbNfI94.png" saved-media-id="aa1xcfn81d0o28e" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="practical-light-afterimage" alt="High-contrast editorial studio photograph of anonymous hands holding a sheet of black paper at the far right while a narrow bone-white beam enters through a cut aperture and leaves a controlled coral and amber afterimage across the frame, left third kept as deep near-black negative space, practical hard light, restrained film grain, no faces, logos, text, or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="-o8t41BcbA" vertical-align="end"><p role="eyebrow">Provisional conference topic</p><display size="lg">Make room<br>for the unexpected</display><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="lg" style="padding-right: 42%;">Creative experimentation is not waiting for lightning. It is building conditions where surprise can appear, be recognized, and become useful.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="BXIZ3SSShi" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="qls7Vu29yQ"><display size="md" font-size="50pt">A perfect plan can only deliver<br><span text-color="accent">what it already knows</span></display><spacer size="20pt"></spacer><grid divider="sm neutral-border"><grid-item id="AuoJBBTJN4" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Efficiency</p><p font-size="lg">Removing variation is valuable when the destination is known—and dangerous when the destination is the question.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="PBMVRhi4A1" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">The creative paradox</p><p font-size="lg">We need enough structure to act, with enough openness to encounter something we did not prescribe.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="_Np8jQTVbx"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="m8DqskFA_p"><h2>Two loops. Two outcomes.</h2><p>Complementary modes: choose the loop that matches what is known.</p><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="7ECTZ_8D6t" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Production loop</p><smart-layout variant="cycle" cell-size="10"><smart-layout-item><h4>Define</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Execute</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Verify</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Repeat</h4></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><p font-size="sm">Protects quality when the destination is known.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="J5oEbJW9tN" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Discovery loop</p><smart-layout variant="cycle" cell-size="10"><smart-layout-item><h4>Frame</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Vary</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Notice</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Select</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Learn</h4></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><p font-size="sm">Creates evidence when the destination is not known.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Confuse the modes and we get polished sameness—or exploration without consequence.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="TCTK_0ycka"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="lny8p3dvzs"><h2>Not a brainstorm. A bounded bet.</h2><p font-size="lg">A useful experiment has edges.</p><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="cwekr6Po4x" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="solid">Question</label></labels><h4>What are we trying to learn?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="yrxTHSLz0R" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="solid">Constants</label></labels><h4>What must remain stable?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="XNSW_t6cDE" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="solid">Variable</label></labels><h4>What changes this time?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="udm6fywKgx" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="solid">Signal</label></labels><h4>What would make the result worth pursuing?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="s_h_vW_-MZ" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="solid">Stop</label></labels><h4>When will we decide?</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="85QdNt_8Zc"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Z4-icj9ppD" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.46" vertical-align="end" colspan="37"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/zlXaxNT7FC_JUZ80qhToy.png" saved-media-id="1hmqybjrh03uj9m" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="practical-light-afterimage" alt="High-contrast overhead editorial studio photograph of anonymous hands interrupting a straight path of black paper with a small glass prism, one hard coral beam diverted into an amber trace with a faint ultraviolet residual afterimage, practical hard light, deep negative space around ordinary cutting and drawing tools, restrained grain, no faces, logos, text, or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"><p role="eyebrow">Deliberate variation</p><h1>Design the interruption</h1><p font-size="lg">Change one thing strongly enough to create evidence, not noise.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="RsrW0Ojr2d" background-color="surface" padding="38pt 32pt" colspan="23"><p role="eyebrow">Change one axis</p><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="Bwta66beku" cell-style="subtle"><h3>Material</h3><p>Translate the idea into another medium.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Lr9WebJ4Ca" cell-style="subtle"><h3>Rule</h3><p>Remove a familiar option or impose an unlikely limit.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="-oEuA8XkA9" cell-style="subtle"><h3>Perspective</h3><p>Let another discipline, audience, or scale reshape the question.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="sm">One interruption at a time keeps the lesson visible.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="YSFiJ61EK-" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="dt4rVXayuh"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative example—not measured conference data</p><h2>One brief, 24 departures</h2><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="TSSGS8DdJn" colspan="15"><h4>Frame</h4><p>Fix one six-word brief, monochrome, and 30 minutes. Change one rule per round.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Z9VAi19qVP" colspan="15"><h4>Generate</h4><formula>4 \times 6 = 24</formula><p>Four rounds create 24 departures.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="xczj_k31gn" colspan="15"><h4>Mark</h4><p>Three reviewers independently mark “surprising” and “usable.”</p></grid-item><grid-item id="vT8mqibs67" colspan="15"><h4>Advance</h4><p>Continue ideas earning both marks from at least two reviewers.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="iTgqq3PFHC"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="o_XANNhydt"><h2>Open a 72-hour aperture</h2><p font-size="lg">Act before the idea becomes precious.</p><smart-layout variant="minimalTimeline" orientation="horizontal" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><h4>Today</h4><p>Write one question and name the constants.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Tomorrow</h4><p>Run three variations with one changed rule.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Within 72 hours</h4><p>Show two people, record their signals, and choose what continues.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><spacer size="16pt"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="PUz2ridco3" background-color="accent" padding="14pt 18pt"><h4>What did the interruption reveal that the plan concealed?</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="2c8VJsD1TL" vertical-align="end" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.52" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/y51aL5DS_jH1dld2ID2jD.png" saved-media-id="qoj0v6qbppcfehj" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="practical-light-afterimage" alt="High-contrast editorial studio photograph of a near-black doorway standing slightly open on the right, a narrow bone-white rectangle of practical hard light crossing the floor, one amber long-exposure line passing through the opening and leaving a faint ultraviolet residual trace, deep uncluttered negative space on the left, restrained film grain, no people, logos, text, or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="7SmFbo4AlK" vertical-align="end"><p role="eyebrow">Protect the promise. Loosen the route.</p><display size="lg">Leave a door open</display><p font-size="lg" style="padding-right: 38%;">Make one constraint explicit. Change one variable. Notice what surprises you. Keep what earns its place.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><h3 role="subheading" style="padding-right: 34%;">The unexpected is not the opposite of rigor. It is what rigor can be designed to discover.</h3></grid-item></grid></section>